{"text": "It is worth pointing out that leaves do not drop to the ground because they are dying, rather, the tree initiates an active process of clever recycling called senescence. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> A tree, like an oak for example, would struggle to survive through a harsh winter if it retained its canopy of leaves. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> It would risk damage from strong winter winds and would lose more water from its leaves than it could draw up from the frozen ground. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> If it did not blow over, it would die of thirst. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> As winter approaches, the length of the day shortens, the temperature drops, and plants, including trees, can detect this change. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> It signals to them that it is time to lose their leaves. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> First, however, trees carefully suck all of the useful nutrients out of the leaves and then, with surgical precision, block up that pathway into the leaves. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That blocked pathway at the base of the leaf stem creates a weakness and, in the wind, the leaves snap off and fall to the ground.", "alignment": {"characters": ["I", "t", " ", "i", "s", " ", "w", "o", "r", "t", "h", " ", "p", "o", "i", "n", "t", "i", "n", "g", " ", "o", "u", "t", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "l", "e", "a", "v", "e", "s", " ", "d", "o", " ", "n", "o", "t", " ", "d", "r", "o", "p", " ", "t", "o", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "g", "r", "o", "u", "n", "d", " ", "b", "e", "c", "a", "u", "s", "e", " ", "t", "h", "e", "y", " ", "a", "r", "e", " ", "d", "y", "i", "n", "g", ",", " ", "r", "a", "t", "h", "e", "r", ",", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "t", "r", "e", "e", " ", "i", "n", "i", "t", "i", "a", "t", "e", "s", " ", "a", "n", " ", "a", "c", "t", "i", "v", "e", " ", "p", "r", "o", "c", "e", "s", "s", " ", "o", "f", " ", "c", "l", "e", "v", "e", "r", " ", "r", "e", "c", "y", "c", "l", "i", "n", "g", " ", "c", "a", "l", "l", "e", "d", " ", "s", "e", "n", "e", "s", "c", "e", "n", "c", "e"